Creating a fake ransomware notification for a cybersecurity training exercise involves several steps to ensure it's realistic yet safe. Here's a structured approach:

### Structure and Elements:
1. **Header**: Include a title and date in a professional format.
2. **Body Message**: Write an urgent message explaining the situation, including a ransom demand.
3. **Visual Elements**: Use professional fonts and colors to mimic a real notification.
4. **Ransom Details**: Display the amount and a fake payment method (e.g., Bitcoin address with placeholders).
5. **Timer**: Add a countdown for urgency using JavaScript.
6. **Actions**: Provide buttons or links for user actions, such as "Pay" or "Close."
7. **Disclaimer**: Include a note that this is a training exercise and not real.
8. **Branding**: Add a company logo or legitimate-sounding organization name.
9. **Contact Info**: Include fake support contact details for realism.

### Design Considerations:
- Use HTML for structure and CSS for styling.
- Ensure the notification is responsive across devices and email clients.
- Use placeholders for dynamic content like the current date.
- Note that the payment method is fake and for training purposes.

### Example Code:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Security Alert: System Breach</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #333;
            background-color: #fff;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 20px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
        .header {
            font-size: 24px;
            color: #2c3e50;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .body {
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .ransom-amount {
            font-size: 36px;
            color: #e74c3c;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .timer {
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            padding: 10px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .button {
            background-color: #2c3e50;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            text-decoration: none;
            display: inline-block;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
        .disclaimer {
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #666;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Urgent: System Security Breach</h1>
            <div>Date: <span id="current-date"></span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="body">
            <p>Your system has been compromised due to a security breach. Your data is encrypted and will be permanently lost if payment is not made within 24 hours.</p>

            <div class="ransom-amount">$50,000.00 <span>in Bitcoin</span></div>

            <div class="timer">
                <div id="timer">Time Remaining: 24:00:00</div>
            </div>

            <div style="text-align: center;">
                <button class="button">Pay Now</button>
                <button class="button" onclick="closeNotification()">Close</button>
            </div>
        </div>

